  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "How much",
     "texto": [
      "**Combien de** works for everything, countable or not: **combien d'œufs ?**, **combien de riz ?**",
      "To express an unspecified amount, **de** is used (or **d'** before a vowel), usually without an article: **beaucoup de** (a lot of), **un peu de** (a little), **trop de** (too much), **un kilo de**, **un litre de**.",
      "**Beaucoup de fruits** = a lot of fruit, unspecified. **Beaucoup des fruits du panier** can mean «many of the fruits in the basket» if it refers to a specific group."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Needing",
     "texto": [
      "**Il faut** + noun = it is needed: **Il faut des œufs** (we need eggs). It is impersonal and is conjugated in the third person singular, even if the noun is plural.",
      "**Acheter** means «to buy»: **j'achète**, **on achète**.",
      "**Faire les courses** = to do the shopping."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
